---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import AssistantSetup from "../components/AssistantSetup.astro";
import MemoDemo from "../components/MemoDemo.astro";
import FilingComparison from "../components/FilingComparison.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="How you write, in every AI you already use — Milton"
  description="Your AI has a case of the Mondays in every new chat. Milton keeps what you wrote, from emails to speeches, so the next draft sounds like you."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
    <div>
      <h1 id="headline">How you write, in every AI you already use.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Your AI has a case of the Mondays in every new chat. Milton keeps what
        you wrote, from emails to speeches, so the next draft sounds like you.
        Yeah, that’d be great.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-aside">
        Everyone else is building superintelligence. We’re asking it to stop
        using em dashes.
      </p>
      <div class="actions action-row">
        <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
          Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <AssistantSetup />
      </div>
    </div>
    <MemoDemo />
  </section>
  <div class="assistant-strip">
    <span class="assistant-label">Works with:</span>
    <nav aria-label="AI setup guides">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#claude">Claude</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#chatgpt">ChatGPT</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#claude-code">Claude Code</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#codex">Codex</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup#cursor">Cursor</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/setup">and more</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
  <section class="section" id="why-milton" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## Why not a memory app</p>
    <h2 id="why-heading">A file for how you write.</h2>
    <FilingComparison />
  </section>
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## How it works</p>
    <h2 id="how-heading">Tell it once. Keep it on file.</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      We distribute the memo. Your AI reads your cover sheet before it writes
      for you; following it is still up to the AI.
    </p>
    <div class="slip-wrap">
      <figure class="sheet slip" aria-labelledby="slip-title">
        <div class="sheet-bar">
          <span id="slip-title">INTEROFFICE ROUTING SLIP</span>
        </div>
        <dl class="slip-fields">
          <div>
            <dt>To:</dt>
            <dd>Every AI you connect</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>From:</dt>
            <dd>You</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Re:</dt>
            <dd>How you write</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <ol class="slip-rows">
          <li class="slip-row">
            <span class="slip-box" aria-hidden="true">
              ✓
            </span>
            <p class="slip-text">
              <strong>Connect.</strong> Add Milton to your AI’s connector
              settings and sign in.
            </p>
            <p class="slip-initials">
              <span class="slip-initials-label">Initials</span>
              <span class="slip-initials-value">You</span>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="slip-row">
            <span class="slip-box" aria-hidden="true">
              ✓
            </span>
            <p class="slip-text">
              <strong>File.</strong> When a draft is right, your AI asks “Save
              this as a sample?” You say yes.
            </p>
            <p class="slip-initials">
              <span class="slip-initials-label">Initials</span>
              <span class="slip-initials-value">You</span>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="slip-row">
            <span class="slip-box" aria-hidden="true">
              ✓
            </span>
            <p class="slip-text">
              <strong>Distribute.</strong> Every new chat starts by reading your
              cover sheet and the report that fits. You don’t have to ask.
            </p>
            <p class="slip-initials">
              <span class="slip-initials-label">Initials</span>
              <span class="slip-initials-value">AI</span>
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </figure>
      <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">
        FILED
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-label="Employee testimonial">
    <figure class="employee-testimonial" id="employee-testimonial">
      <blockquote>
        “Milton lets me say ‘Did you get that memo?’ to software. I have never
        felt more qualified for management.”
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Michael Bolton</strong>
        <span>Senior Founding AI Forward Deployed Product Engineer</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ul class="social-proof">
      <li>Would recommend: 1 of 1 founders.</li>
      <li>Reduced rewrites by an amount we did not measure.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">## A few things to know</p>
    <h2 id="faq-heading">Before you connect.</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>What does Milton keep, and what does it never touch?</summary>
      <p>
        Only what you approve: samples of your writing, kept word for word, and
        the rules you ask for, stored as your AI sends them. Milton never
        rewrites a rule or a sample. It never reads your inbox, your files, or
        your conversations.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Couldn’t I just use a Markdown file in a synced folder?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Milton handles the connections and picks samples for the job. We
        added a cover sheet and made it a recurring expense.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I take my writing and leave?</summary>
      <p>
        We won’t take your stapler. The source is public, and you can run Milton
        yourself. Download your rules and samples as TPS.md. Disconnect an AI
        and Milton refuses it at once. We’d prefer you keep paying us, but
        apparently that’s not a retention strategy.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/zoneofdanger/milton">Read the source ↗</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it useful if I only use Claude?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. Keep one voice across conversations with the same AI, with samples
        it can imitate instead of adjectives it has to interpret. Connecting
        another AI later is optional.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which AIs can I connect?</summary>
      <p>
        Milton uses MCP. Your AI needs support for a remote MCP server, sign-in,
        and both reading and saving through tools. Availability depends on your
        AI, plan, and workspace settings.{" "}
        <a href="/setup">Check the setup guide before signing up.</a>
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What’s the cover sheet? What’s a report?</summary>
      <p>
        The cover sheet holds the rules true of all your writing and an index of
        five reports: email, chat, post, document, and speech. Each report holds
        the samples you approved for that kind of writing, then its rules. Your
        AI handles the filing; you don’t manage a memo list. The names are an
        Office Space reference. The paperwork is less demanding.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will my AI always write like me?</summary>
      <p>
        Not always. Milton keeps the samples and rules available. Your AI reads
        them before it writes; it still decides how closely to follow them.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What if Milton is down?</summary>
      <p>
        Your AI writes like itself for a while. You’ll notice. Your cover sheet
        and reports stay on file: a failed read loses nothing, and nothing was
        ever saved without your yes. When Milton is back, ask your AI to read
        the memo again.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details id="why-this-exists">
      <summary>Why does this exist?</summary>
      <p>
        Peter wanted his AIs to write like him. Somehow he ended up building
        them a filing department.
      </p>
      <p class="eyebrow">## An imaginary productivity review</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> Walk us through a typical session.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> First I explain how I like to work. Then I remind
        it. Then it apologizes. Then I explain that I don’t need the apology.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Reviewer:</strong> How much actual work gets done?
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Me:</strong> About fifteen minutes.
      </p>
    </details>
  </section>
  <section class="closing">
    <p class="eyebrow">## Did you get that memo?</p>
    <h2>Let’s put that in a memo.</h2>
    <p>
      We did not build superintelligence. We built a filing department. Cover
      sheets are now required.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">
      Try Milton free <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  :where(h1, h2, p, figure) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* No paragraph ends on a lone word. Scoped to this page, so the demo's
     typed lines keep plain wrapping. */
  p,
  blockquote {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  /* The hero is its own layer above the sections that follow, so the setup
     popover is never drawn under the filing comparison's notes and cabinet
     (their highest layer is 10). */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 11;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-hero);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .hero-aside {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .actions {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .assistant-strip {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .assistant-label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
  }
  .assistant-strip ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 var(--space-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .assistant-strip li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  /* Even separators between names; the dot is decoration, not read aloud. */
  .assistant-strip li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "·";
    content: "·" / "";
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
  }
  .assistant-strip a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .section h2 {
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
  }
  .section h2 span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .section-lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
  }
  /* How it works: an interoffice routing slip across the container. */
  .slip-wrap {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .slip {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .slip-fields {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--sheet-padding);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    font: var(--text-small) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
  }
  .slip-fields > div {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  /* The dot between fields is decoration, not read aloud. */
  .slip-fields > div:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "·";
    content: "·" / "";
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .slip-fields dt {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .slip-fields dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .slip-rows {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: slip;
  }
  .slip-row {
    counter-increment: slip;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) calc(
        var(--space-16) * 1.75
      );
    grid-template-areas: "num box text initials";
    align-items: stretch;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .slip-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .slip-row::before {
    grid-area: num;
    content: "0" counter(slip);
    align-self: center;
    padding-inline: var(--sheet-padding) var(--space-4);
    color: var(--muted);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
  }
  .slip-box {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: var(--space-6);
    height: var(--space-6);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--surface);
    font: var(--text-body) / 1 var(--font-mono);
    grid-area: box;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .slip-text {
    grid-area: text;
    align-self: center;
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6) var(--space-5) var(--space-5);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .slip-text strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .slip-initials {
    grid-area: initials;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .slip-initials-label {
    color: var(--muted);
    font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .slip-initials-value {
    font: italic var(--text-lead) / var(--leading-heading) var(--font-form);
  }
  /* A rubber stamp across the slip's lower edge, below the "AI" initials.
     Decorative only. */
  .stamp {
    position: absolute;
    right: var(--space-3);
    bottom: calc(-1 * var(--space-5));
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-5);
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline: 1px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: calc(var(--space-2) / 2);
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.45;
    transform: rotate(-8deg);
    font: var(--text-section) / 1 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .slip-fields {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .slip-fields > div:not(:last-child)::after {
      display: none;
    }
    .slip-row {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas:
        "box text"
        "box initials";
      column-gap: var(--space-4);
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--sheet-padding);
    }
    .slip-row::before {
      display: none;
    }
    .slip-box {
      align-self: start;
    }
    .slip-text {
      padding: 0;
    }
    .slip-text::before {
      content: "0" counter(slip) " ";
      color: var(--muted);
      font: var(--text-caption) / var(--leading-label) var(--font-mono);
    }
    .slip-initials {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      margin-top: var(--space-3);
      padding: var(--space-2) 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 1px dashed var(--hairline);
    }
    .stamp {
      font-size: var(--text-subtitle);
    }
  }
  .employee-testimonial blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
    font: var(--font-display-weight) var(--text-section) /
      var(--leading-heading) var(--font-display);
  }
  .employee-testimonial figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  .employee-testimonial figcaption span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  /* Fine print where a case study would show its metrics: plain lines under
     the caption, set off by a hairline, one column each across the container. */
  .social-proof {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-8);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    list-style: none;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  .social-proof li {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .faq details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }
  .faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style-position: outside;
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .faq details p {
    margin-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  /* The section's divider closes the last item, as the next item's border
     closes the others, so the list ends on the item rhythm. */
  .section.faq {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }
  .closing h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
  }
  .closing p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (min-width: 861px) and (max-width: 1100px) {
    .hero {
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-10);
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .assistant-strip {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
    .assistant-label {
      min-height: auto;
    }
    .section,
    .closing {
      padding-block: var(--space-12);
    }
    .hero {
      padding-block: var(--space-10);
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
    .intro {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
      margin-top: var(--space-5);
    }
    .actions .button {
      padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    }
    .section-lead {
      font-size: var(--text-body);
    }
    .social-proof {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
